WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Fixing the waters. Things with the water. So now, today, there are also things with the water. But instead of fixing the area where there will be seas, now God will turn this water into a source of life.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:35.000
And God says, Let the water produce sheres. Sheres means in Hebrew, we use sheres as worm today. But in Hebrew, sheres means not only a worm or something that creeps, but anything that has a motion on its own.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:49.000
Anything that could move, that the motion is up to it. In other words, in distinction with a tree. A tree does not move. I mean, it grows, but it doesn't move from place to place. Now, sheres is anything that has a motion, that could move.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:01:04.000
An insect or anything that moves. So therefore, sheres is a very general term. Includes anything that has the power to move on its own. Yes? So therefore, do not forget the word sheres. It's a very important word.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:24.000
A sheres, which has a nefesh, a soul, haya, of life. In other words, now God creates life in a biological sense. Not only as vegetation, but a more complicated life, the kind of life that allows that organism to move.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:47.000
So therefore, God creates nefesh haya, a living life, a living soul. Yes? And also, you could also use the word soul for this. Because in Hebrew, the word soul is more general than in English. In the sense, it doesn't mean only a spirit, but means an organization that allows you to function.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:02:07.000
You know, to function in a particular way. In other words, it's more generic than in English. You see, so that's why here you find that the animals also they have a kind of a nefesh. Because they have a kind of organism, an organization, that allows them to function and to move and to do things. So that is a nefesh. Yes?

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:28.000
By yom elohim, it's a mind that shares nefesh haya. A sheres that is a nefesh haya, or has a nefesh haya. And also, you know, a derivation, an instance of this, is of Yahweh fal'aarez. Some of them will be birds, who also fly, are part of nefesh haya.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:29.000
By yom elohim, it's a nefesh haya. And also, you know, a derivation, an instance of this, is of Yahweh fal'aarez. Some of them will be birds, who also fly, are part of nefesh haya. And also, you know, a derivation, an instance of this, is of Yahweh fal'aarez. Some of them will be birds, who also fly, are part of nefesh haya.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:18.000
So, if we want to be very, very specific, nefesh is life, you know, biology. This is nefesh. And so, in this way, we, men, are not the only animals who have nefesh. All living things have nefesh.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:28.000
However, then there is ruach, and then there is also neshamah. And neshamah is the exclusive patrimony of men. Only men have neshamah, but not nefesh. Clear?

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:43.000
Yes. Ruach haya, for Noah, says. Also, it's for animals. But not for neshamah, it's the only thing which is not for...

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:49.000
I like to share this, it would be like a one-celled animal, like an ant. Like an amoeba.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:53.000
Yes. Then the nefesh haya would be one that's a lot more complicated.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:04:07.000
That's right. Yes, but you see, the truth of the matter is, that the smaller we go into nature, we see the greatest complication. Everything is a world in itself, you know.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:15.000
And even if you go to analyze the small of all cells, there's also a kind of nefesh there that controls it. It's almost a miracle.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:25.000
Everything, you know, when you study it very, very carefully, you see that the smaller world is as miraculous as the largest of all constellations.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:37.000
So, this nefesh, it's all over the nefesh. It happened to me, I mean, once I saw a program showing about the world, the infinite world, the small world, you know.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:46.000
And you see the cut things, you come to see things which are a millionth, you know, of an inch.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:52.000
They have microscopes today that you could project one million more at size.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:57.000
And they see the things, and they see that it's also composed of other things, and has a kind of motion, and has this, and so on.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:01.000
So, we don't know, you know what I mean. The world is a very complex world.

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:13.000
And probably, it's true, everything, every shares is in itself a nefesh haya, with a whole program, and a whole, like, computing machine, yes, in an infinitesimal size.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:14.000
Sir?

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:19.000
Is he referring to the marine life, like, a feeling, like it says over here?

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:22.000
Share is nefesh.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:24.000
Is he referring to the marine life right now?

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:32.000
Well, I have to tell you, without being scientific, today's science recognizes that the beginning of life is in the water, you see.

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:36.000
So, life begins in the water, you see.

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:37.000
We already have vegetation.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:41.000
But, yes, that's true.

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:47.000
But, you know, the world, the animal life, yes, it begins in the sea.

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:58.000
And this is, you know, this is acknowledged by science today, and this is probably what the Bible is telling you here, that the beginning of animal life, it is from the sea.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:09.000
And we know that the first cells come out from the water, yes, the simplest and the most essential cells that come from, this is the beginning of life, is in the water.

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:16.000
Today, by the way, the largest, in the sea, it has a much larger population than the earth.

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:24.000
There's more, different kind of vegetation, there's much more vegetation in the sea, there's also much more animal life in the sea than there is on the earth.

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:25.000
This is a fact.

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:26.000
It's amazing.

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:27.000
You know, but...

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:36.000
They say that for every animal there is on earth, they have a match in the sea.

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:37.000
That's right.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:38.000
They even started to match them.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:40.000
That's right, but I think there is more than this.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:43.000
Even there is more in the sea than there is on earth.

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:44.000
Alright?

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:48.000
But the beginning of life, according to the Bible, it comes from the sea.

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:58.000
Now,

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:08.000
Let the water produce sheres, nefesh haya, and every sheres should have his own nefesh haya, his own organization of life.

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:13.000
And also, birds will be able to fly.

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:19.000
That's very important, this pasuk.

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:25.000
And let me tell you how I studied this pasuk, and I'm following this expression of Rabbi Shlomo Ben Melech, which I mentioned to you last week.

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:26.000
Last week.

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:39.000
Now, let me translate this and tell you how I explained this, according to this hacham I mentioned to you last week.

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:53.000
The great fishes refer to the monsters, to the antediluvian monsters, the dinosaurs and things like this.

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:55.000
And it's called tanninim.

00:07:55.000 --> 00:08:05.000
Now, tanninim were known in antiquity, and as a matter of fact, among the goyim, they thought that those monsters were not created by the gods, in plural.

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:06.000
You know?

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:10.000
They were so great and so monstrous that no god could have created this.

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:12.000
That's why I explained once.

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:14.000
Do you remember when Moshe Rabbeinu comes to Barov?

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:18.000
He throws the shere, you know, the mate.

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:19.000
And what has to become the mate?

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:20.000
Do you remember this step?

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:21.000
Nahash.

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:22.000
No, tanninim.

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:23.000
Tanninim?

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:24.000
Tanninim.

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:25.000
Ah!

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:29.000
You're right and you're wrong, and they're right and they're wrong.

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:33.000
When he came to the Jewish people, he throws the shere, why it became nahash.

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:37.000
When he goes to Barov, it becomes tannin.

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:38.000
Why?

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:43.000
For the Jewish people, they wanted to know whether he's a prophet or not.

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:45.000
A small miracle, that's sufficient.

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:46.000
Nahash.

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:50.000
But when he goes to Barov, nahash, that's not enough for him.

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:54.000
Why he let tannin become a dinosaur.

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:56.000
A dinosaur becomes, you see?

00:08:56.000 --> 00:08:57.000
That's the point.

00:08:57.000 --> 00:09:01.000
There with Barov, nahash, that's not enough for him.

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:04.000
He took the mate, why he let tannin.

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:07.000
It became a dinosaur.

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:08.000
So here...

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:10.000
Why the dinosaurs became extinct?

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:11.000
Don't ask me.

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:12.000
Pardon?

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:14.000
Why the dinosaurs became extinct?

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:17.000
That is a nice explanation.

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:21.000
But also, I tell you another explanation which I gave.

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:30.000
Let me give you another explanation.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:37.000
Why the tannin were unable to survive.

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:43.000
And that is a simple explanation.

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:46.000
The tannin were very, very powerful.

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:47.000
Very strong.

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:50.000
Each tannin in itself, yes?

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:54.000
Had more power and more strength than anything else.

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:56.000
But they were unable to reproduce.

00:09:56.000 --> 00:10:00.000
And this is a very good musal for us to know.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:02.000
Sometimes we say, well, I'm very religious.

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:04.000
I know a lot of Torah.

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:05.000
I know a lot of this.

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:06.000
I'm strong.

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:07.000
I'm religious and so on.

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:09.000
But that's not important.

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:13.000
If you want to survive, you have to be able to reproduce.

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:16.000
And if you don't reproduce, no matter how strong you are,

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:20.000
the history of that particular individual cannot be very long.

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:22.000
We have to be able to reproduce.

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:28.000
This is what the sign says.

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:30.000
They were unable to reproduce.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:32.000
That was the problem with the tannin.

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:34.000
They produced very little.

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:36.000
They could not adapt.

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:38.000
The point is that they could not reproduce.

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:42.000
This is the standard expression today.

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:44.000
They were unable to reproduce.

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:49.000
They were unable to reproduce.

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:57.000
Not only was it difficult, but whatever the reason is,

00:10:57.000 --> 00:10:59.000
they were unable to reproduce.

00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:00.000
There are many reasons.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:03.000
And because they were unable to reproduce,

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:09.000
I don't know.

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:17.000
Gentlemen, it's unimportant whether they were able to reproduce or not.

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:19.000
I mean, really, that's not the point.

00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:21.000
Just a second.

00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:26.000
Yes, a question?

00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:29.000
Yeah, I wanted to ask you, why would they go down to the surface

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:31.000
if they weren't allowed to reproduce?

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:33.000
No, but I didn't say that they were not allowed.

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:35.000
I said that they were unable.

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:37.000
Now, what was the reason for their being?

00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:39.000
I don't know.

00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:41.000
Why do you get the idea that they weren't able to reproduce?

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:42.000
That's why.

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:44.000
Anyhow, gentlemen, please.

00:11:44.000 --> 00:11:45.000
What did you get?

00:11:46.000 --> 00:11:47.000
Not bad.

00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:51.000
In the name of God,

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:54.000
in the name of God, the great tannins,

00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:56.000
and every living soul,

00:11:56.000 --> 00:11:58.000
and all the living souls,

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:02.000
that is able to creep, to move,

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:06.000
and every soul has its own species,

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:08.000
has its own type,

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:10.000
has its own characteristics,

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:14.000
and every bird,

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:18.000
Now, why does it here say the word,

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:20.000
the word,

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:22.000
creation?

00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:24.000
Do you remember that I mentioned before,

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:26.000
in the name of this Rabbi,

00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:28.000
that the word, in Hebrew,

00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:30.000
it applies whenever it's something which is

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:32.000
difficult to grasp,

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:34.000
something that we cannot understand,

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:36.000
something which is very

00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:39.000
elusive.

00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:40.000
That is the word, bara.

00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:41.000
Like for instance,

00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:44.000
we don't understand exactly what does it mean the other word, bara.

00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:45.000
So also here, he says,

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:46.000
why is this here, bara?

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:49.000
Because bara does not refer only to the tanninim,

00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:51.000
but refers to the nefesh hachayah.

00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:52.000
That's the way it's said.

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:57.000
It refers, the word, bara,

00:12:57.000 --> 00:13:00.000
to the creation of every living soul.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:02.000
Now, how does everything live?

00:13:02.000 --> 00:13:04.000
What is the soul, the organism,

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:07.000
or the system of every living thing?

00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:08.000
This is difficult to understand.

00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:10.000
And this is the bara.

00:13:10.000 --> 00:13:12.000
bara does not refer only to the tanninim,

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:14.000
but also to the nefesh hachayah.

00:13:14.000 --> 00:13:17.000
In other words, bara refers to every nefesh.

00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:19.000
And because here it creates something new,

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:21.000
namely that there is such a thing,

00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:22.000
that they have a nefesh,

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:25.000
and this nefesh enables them to move,

00:13:25.000 --> 00:13:27.000
and nefesh lamineru,

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:29.000
and every nefesh has its own system,

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:30.000
and its own characteristic,

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:31.000
this is a bara.

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:34.000
This is something which is difficult for us to grasp.

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:37.000
And that's why the verb, bara, is applied to...

00:13:43.000 --> 00:13:44.000
No, no, it doesn't mean this.

00:13:45.000 --> 00:13:46.000
Oh, right, he can, he says.

00:13:46.000 --> 00:13:48.000
That's why it's here, he says, right, he can.

00:13:48.000 --> 00:13:50.000
This is the question, you know,

00:13:50.000 --> 00:13:51.000
by the way, excuse me.

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:54.000
The septuagenous, you know, the goyim,

00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:56.000
the Christians, they have a Bible,

00:13:56.000 --> 00:13:57.000
that they took from us,

00:13:57.000 --> 00:13:59.000
because at one time the Jews used to speak Greek.

00:13:59.000 --> 00:14:01.000
A Bible, no, no, the Old Testament,

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:03.000
which they took from us,

00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:04.000
but they didn't take it from us in Hebrew,

00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:05.000
because they could not read Hebrew,

00:14:05.000 --> 00:14:07.000
but they took it in Greek.

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:08.000
And this is called a septuagenous,

00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:09.000
septuagenous means sheveim,

00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:11.000
because the word sheveim, shekeim,

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:13.000
that translated the Bible to Talmai,

00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:14.000
a king in Egypt.

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:15.000
This is a fact.

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:18.000
Now, this Bible, they took it,

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:20.000
but then they changed many things with time and so on.

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:21.000
Then it is interesting,

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:23.000
in that Bible it says like this,

00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:30.000
Baraycheh, it says Baraycheh there.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:32.000
And after, that's right,

00:14:32.000 --> 00:14:33.000
it says Baraycheh.

00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:35.000
And many people say,

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:36.000
well, all the time it says Baraycheh,

00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:37.000
also here it should say Baraycheh.

00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:40.000
The Ramban says,

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:41.000
you cannot say here Baraycheh, why?

00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:43.000
Because the Taminim didn't last forever.

00:14:43.000 --> 00:14:46.000
Baraycheh is only when something

00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:48.000
is going to remain forever.

00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:49.000
So, sometimes, you know,

00:14:49.000 --> 00:14:50.000
when I was here you could see

00:14:50.000 --> 00:14:52.000
how the goyim mind worked.

00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:54.000
They see all of the time Baraycheh,

00:14:54.000 --> 00:14:56.000
so they inserted also Baraycheh.

00:14:56.000 --> 00:14:58.000
But they don't understand the meaning of,

00:14:58.000 --> 00:14:59.000
you know, of Baraycheh.

00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:01.000
So Baraycheh, it means what?

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:03.000
Something that is going to remain forever.

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:04.000
Baraycheh means so it was.

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:05.000
Sir?

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:07.000
What is the difference between,

00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:08.000
if there is any difference,

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:13.000
between Nebuchadnezzar and Shedes?

00:15:13.000 --> 00:15:15.000
Oh, Shedes means something that could move.

00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:17.000
Now, very good.

00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:19.000
No, it's a good question.

00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:20.000
I'm going to tell you the difference.

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:22.000
Shedes, in theory,

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:23.000
you could say something that could move.

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:25.000
But also the moon could move, you know.

00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:27.000
A stone could move.

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:28.000
I mean, you throw the stone and move.

00:15:28.000 --> 00:15:30.000
But Nevesh Hayah,

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:32.000
it means that it has a Nevesh Hayah

00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:34.000
that allows it to move.

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:36.000
That its motion is independent.

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:38.000
It has its own motion.

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:39.000
What?

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:41.000
It has a soul.

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:42.000
It has a soul.

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:43.000
But the word, just the word,

00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:45.000
that's the difference.

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:46.000
That is the difference.

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:48.000
Now, Shedes, if you just take it

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:49.000
from a grammatical point of view,

00:15:49.000 --> 00:15:50.000
you could say,

00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:51.000
well, anything that moves is Shedes.

00:15:51.000 --> 00:15:53.000
Then when you say maybe a stone also,

00:15:53.000 --> 00:15:55.000
you may call it grammatically Shedes.

00:15:55.000 --> 00:15:56.000
You see?

00:15:56.000 --> 00:15:57.000
Because it moves also.

00:15:57.000 --> 00:15:58.000
You kick it and it moves.

00:15:58.000 --> 00:15:59.000
You see?

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:01.000
So now, therefore it says Nevesh Hayah.

00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:03.000
A Shedes that has a Nevesh Hayah.

00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:05.000
A Shedes that its motion

00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:08.000
is the result of its own self.

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:10.000
Of its own life organization.

00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:11.000
In this way,

00:16:11.000 --> 00:16:12.000
we distinguish between the Shedes,

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:13.000
the Nevesh Hayah,

00:16:13.000 --> 00:16:15.000
and say, I don't know,

00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:17.000
water that runs through,

00:16:17.000 --> 00:16:18.000
a stream of water also runs.

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:20.000
But that's not Shedes Nevesh Hayah.

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:21.000
You understand?

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:22.000
Although it moves.

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:23.000
You understand?

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:25.000
Because the motion is not of its own.

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:26.000
Am I getting,

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:27.000
is it getting too complicated?

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:28.000
No.

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:29.000
No?

00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:30.000
Are you saying that the word,

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:32.000
or intangible or something?

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:33.000
Intangible, yes.

00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:36.000
Isn't it tangible?

00:16:36.000 --> 00:16:37.000
You're right,

00:16:37.000 --> 00:16:38.000
but I said in the Bible.

00:16:38.000 --> 00:16:39.000
No.

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:42.000
Is it intangible?

00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:43.000
Yes,

00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:44.000
but this is only for the Bible.

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:47.000
Gentlemen,

00:16:47.000 --> 00:16:48.000
please let me continue.

00:16:51.000 --> 00:16:54.000
Vayvarech otam Elohim lemor.

00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:55.000
And God blessed

00:16:55.000 --> 00:16:57.000
this Shedes,

00:16:57.000 --> 00:16:58.000
Nevesh Hayah,

00:16:58.000 --> 00:16:59.000
in the same way

00:16:59.000 --> 00:17:00.000
that He blessed man.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:01.000
And He tells,

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:03.000
perum huyvoh.

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:05.000
Multiply and become many.

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:07.000
Umir uret amayim bayamim.

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:09.000
Fill the waters of the seas.

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:11.000
Ve'ahov yirev ba'aret.

00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:13.000
And the birds should also multiply.

00:17:13.000 --> 00:17:14.000
Now,

00:17:14.000 --> 00:17:15.000
what does it mean that God blessed them

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:16.000
and told them multiply?

00:17:16.000 --> 00:17:17.000
It doesn't say that God,

00:17:17.000 --> 00:17:18.000
you know,

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:19.000
called the animals

00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:20.000
and said, you know,

00:17:20.000 --> 00:17:22.000
stretched His hand

00:17:22.000 --> 00:17:23.000
and He says, you know,

00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:24.000
perum huyvoh.

00:17:24.000 --> 00:17:25.000
It doesn't mean like this.

00:17:25.000 --> 00:17:26.000
It means,

00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:27.000
God blessed them means

00:17:27.000 --> 00:17:29.000
God gave them the power

00:17:29.000 --> 00:17:31.000
to reproduce.

00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:32.000
Not only God made them

00:17:32.000 --> 00:17:34.000
living things.

00:17:34.000 --> 00:17:36.000
Vayvarech otam Elohim.

00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:37.000
God gave them a blessing.

00:17:37.000 --> 00:17:38.000
What does it mean,

00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:39.000
gave them a blessing?

00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:41.000
He gave them the power

00:17:41.000 --> 00:17:42.000
to multiply.

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:45.000
They have to use it

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:46.000
Yes?

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:47.000
But the point is

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:48.000
that God is not

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:49.000
verachah in the sense

00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:50.000
that you,

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:51.000
where usually,

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:52.000
you know,

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:53.000
usually in the sense

00:17:53.000 --> 00:17:54.000
that somebody puts his hand

00:17:54.000 --> 00:17:55.000
over you

00:17:55.000 --> 00:17:56.000
and says, you know,

00:17:56.000 --> 00:17:57.000
baruch atameh vo'echa

00:17:57.000 --> 00:17:58.000
or whatever it is.

00:17:58.000 --> 00:17:59.000
No.

00:17:59.000 --> 00:18:00.000
No.

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:01.000
It means that God gave them

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:02.000
a concrete power,

00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:03.000
the power of reproduction.

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:04.000
We're going to see.

00:18:04.000 --> 00:18:05.000
We're going to see.

00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:06.000
Wait.

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:07.000
We're going to see.

00:18:07.000 --> 00:18:08.000
But perum huyvoh

00:18:08.000 --> 00:18:09.000
here doesn't mean

00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:10.000
a commandment that says

00:18:10.000 --> 00:18:11.000
God over there,

00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:12.000
you know,

00:18:12.000 --> 00:18:13.000
the snake going there.

00:18:13.000 --> 00:18:14.000
No.

00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:15.000
God is giving animal

00:18:15.000 --> 00:18:16.000
the power

00:18:16.000 --> 00:18:17.000
to reproduce.

00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:24.000
Well,

00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:25.000
I really don't know

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:26.000
for this you have to ask.

00:18:36.000 --> 00:18:37.000
I don't know,

00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:38.000
really.

00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:39.000
Real life,

00:18:39.000 --> 00:18:40.000
but also

00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:42.000
a life that comes

00:18:42.000 --> 00:18:43.000
from the earth,

00:18:43.000 --> 00:18:44.000
a more complex life.

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:46.000
And every nefesh haya,

00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:48.000
toseh ha'ales nefesh haya,

00:18:48.000 --> 00:18:49.000
but every nefesh haya,

00:18:49.000 --> 00:18:51.000
every living organism

00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:53.000
should be lemina,

00:18:53.000 --> 00:18:55.000
according to its own species,

00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:57.000
according to its own laws.

00:18:57.000 --> 00:18:59.000
In other words,

00:18:59.000 --> 00:19:02.000
life is not uniform.

00:19:02.000 --> 00:19:03.000
There are,

00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:05.000
every organism has

00:19:05.000 --> 00:19:08.000
its own laws.

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:09.000
And therefore,

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:10.000
nefesh haya,

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:11.000
lemina,

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:13.000
according to its own species,

00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:15.000
according to its own laws.

00:19:17.000 --> 00:19:18.000
Behemoth,

00:19:18.000 --> 00:19:20.000
there will be behemoth.

00:19:20.000 --> 00:19:21.000
Baremes,

00:19:21.000 --> 00:19:23.000
behemoth is

00:19:23.000 --> 00:19:24.000
animals

00:19:24.000 --> 00:19:28.000
that could become domesticated.

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:29.000
Baremes means

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:32.000
things that creep.

00:19:32.000 --> 00:19:33.000
Behaito'eres,

00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:35.000
it means the wild animals

00:19:35.000 --> 00:19:36.000
from the land.

00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:37.000
Lemina,

00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:39.000
and every nefesh of this

00:19:39.000 --> 00:19:41.000
has its own laws,

00:19:41.000 --> 00:19:44.000
its own peculiarities.

00:19:44.000 --> 00:19:45.000
Bahichen,

00:19:45.000 --> 00:19:47.000
and so it was.

00:19:47.000 --> 00:19:49.000
It means it remains like this.

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:50.000
Whereas in the other one,

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:51.000
it doesn't say bahichen.

00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:53.000
Vaya'as elohim,

00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:55.000
et hayata'ares lemina,

00:19:55.000 --> 00:19:56.000
he made God

00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:57.000
the different kinds

00:19:57.000 --> 00:19:59.000
of living things.

00:20:03.000 --> 00:20:04.000
At the end of the six days,

00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:05.000
says God,

00:20:05.000 --> 00:20:06.000
kitob again,

00:20:06.000 --> 00:20:07.000
and then I will explain

00:20:07.000 --> 00:20:08.000
what does it mean kitob.

00:20:09.000 --> 00:20:12.000
Now,

00:20:12.000 --> 00:20:14.000
in the sixth day,

00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:17.000
God decides to,

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:19.000
from this complex life,

00:20:19.000 --> 00:20:20.000
to make something

00:20:20.000 --> 00:20:22.000
much more complex.

00:20:22.000 --> 00:20:23.000
And we are going to see

00:20:23.000 --> 00:20:24.000
what is this complexity.

00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:30.000
Let us make a man

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:31.000
in our image

00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:32.000
just like us.

00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:33.000
I will explain to you

00:20:33.000 --> 00:20:34.000
in a second.

00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:36.000
But you are saying

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:37.000
the word morally.

00:20:37.000 --> 00:20:38.000
Yes,

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:39.000
I will explain to you.

00:20:43.000 --> 00:20:44.000
Vaya'as elohim,

00:20:44.000 --> 00:20:45.000
God says,

00:20:45.000 --> 00:20:46.000
na'ase adam

00:20:46.000 --> 00:20:47.000
vesalmenu kibmutenu.

00:20:47.000 --> 00:20:48.000
Let us make a man

00:20:48.000 --> 00:20:49.000
in our image

00:20:49.000 --> 00:20:50.000
just like us.

00:20:54.000 --> 00:20:55.000
Vaya'as elohim,

00:20:55.000 --> 00:20:56.000
a man will have

00:20:56.000 --> 00:20:58.000
a right

00:20:58.000 --> 00:21:00.000
to control.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:01.000
Vaya'as elohim means

00:21:01.000 --> 00:21:02.000
to control.

00:21:02.000 --> 00:21:03.000
Vaya'as elohim,

00:21:04.000 --> 00:21:05.000
the life of the sea,

00:21:05.000 --> 00:21:07.000
of the birds,

00:21:07.000 --> 00:21:10.000
and the animals,

00:21:10.000 --> 00:21:11.000
and anything which is

00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:12.000
on the earth.

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:14.000
Everything that

00:21:14.000 --> 00:21:15.000
creeps on the earth.

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:16.000
In other words,

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:17.000
man will be able

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:18.000
to control,

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:19.000
to dominate,

00:21:19.000 --> 00:21:20.000
to have a right

00:21:20.000 --> 00:21:21.000
over all creatures.

00:21:21.000 --> 00:21:22.000
Now,

00:21:22.000 --> 00:21:23.000
there are several questions

00:21:23.000 --> 00:21:24.000
in this verse

00:21:24.000 --> 00:21:25.000
which are very,

00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:26.000
very difficult.

00:21:26.000 --> 00:21:27.000
The first is,

00:21:27.000 --> 00:21:28.000
na'ase adam vesalmenu.

00:21:28.000 --> 00:21:29.000
Let us make a man

00:21:29.000 --> 00:21:30.000
in our own image.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:32.000
Why is it plural?

00:21:34.000 --> 00:21:35.000
Now,

00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:36.000
the Christians,

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:38.000
they take this verse

00:21:38.000 --> 00:21:39.000
and they say,

00:21:39.000 --> 00:21:40.000
from here,

00:21:40.000 --> 00:21:41.000
we have to bring a proof

00:21:41.000 --> 00:21:42.000
that the trinity,

00:21:42.000 --> 00:21:43.000
there is more than one God.

00:21:44.000 --> 00:21:45.000
Why?

00:21:45.000 --> 00:21:46.000
Because it says here,

00:21:46.000 --> 00:21:48.000
na'ase adam vesalmenu.

00:21:48.000 --> 00:21:49.000
Let us make it.

00:21:49.000 --> 00:21:50.000
So obviously,

00:21:50.000 --> 00:21:51.000
there is more

00:21:51.000 --> 00:21:52.000
than one God.

00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:53.000
That is the

00:21:53.000 --> 00:21:54.000
Christian explanation.

00:21:54.000 --> 00:21:55.000
This is one of the,

00:21:55.000 --> 00:21:56.000
of the,

00:21:56.000 --> 00:21:57.000
you know,

00:21:57.000 --> 00:21:59.000
the verses that they bring.

00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:00.000
Because it says,

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:01.000
na'ase adam.

00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:02.000
Yes?

00:22:02.000 --> 00:22:03.000
What is the answer

00:22:03.000 --> 00:22:04.000
that royalty speaks

00:22:04.000 --> 00:22:05.000
and says,

00:22:05.000 --> 00:22:06.000
we?

00:22:06.000 --> 00:22:07.000
That is a simple answer.

00:22:07.000 --> 00:22:08.000
This is what we say.

00:22:08.000 --> 00:22:09.000
In other words,

00:22:09.000 --> 00:22:10.000
God is talking to himself.

00:22:11.000 --> 00:22:12.000
And in the following,

00:22:12.000 --> 00:22:13.000
it shows here,

00:22:13.000 --> 00:22:14.000
the pre-eminence

00:22:14.000 --> 00:22:15.000
of man.

00:22:16.000 --> 00:22:17.000
Of course,

00:22:17.000 --> 00:22:18.000
when God created,

00:22:18.000 --> 00:22:19.000
everything that God created,

00:22:20.000 --> 00:22:21.000
God planned that before.

00:22:22.000 --> 00:22:23.000
Before He created

00:22:23.000 --> 00:22:24.000
the world,

00:22:24.000 --> 00:22:25.000
before He created the animals,

00:22:25.000 --> 00:22:26.000
everything is planned

00:22:26.000 --> 00:22:27.000
by God.

00:22:27.000 --> 00:22:28.000
But it's not written

00:22:28.000 --> 00:22:29.000
in the Torah.

00:22:29.000 --> 00:22:30.000
You know?

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:31.000
Because things are not

00:22:31.000 --> 00:22:32.000
as important.

00:22:32.000 --> 00:22:33.000
But when it comes

00:22:33.000 --> 00:22:34.000
to man,

00:22:34.000 --> 00:22:36.000
God makes us know

00:22:36.000 --> 00:22:38.000
that He planned man.

00:22:38.000 --> 00:22:39.000
In other words,

00:22:39.000 --> 00:22:40.000
and therefore,

00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:41.000
God speaks to himself.

00:22:41.000 --> 00:22:42.000
How does God

00:22:42.000 --> 00:22:43.000
speak to himself?

00:22:43.000 --> 00:22:44.000
He speaks to himself

00:22:44.000 --> 00:22:45.000
in plural.

00:22:45.000 --> 00:22:46.000
You know?

00:22:46.000 --> 00:22:47.000
His royalty

00:22:47.000 --> 00:22:48.000
speaks in plural.

00:22:49.000 --> 00:22:50.000
So therefore,

00:22:50.000 --> 00:22:51.000
God, when He's speaking

00:22:51.000 --> 00:22:52.000
to himself,

00:22:52.000 --> 00:22:53.000
He says,

00:22:53.000 --> 00:22:54.000
na'ase adam.

00:22:54.000 --> 00:22:55.000
You see?

00:22:55.000 --> 00:22:56.000
Because that is,

00:22:56.000 --> 00:22:57.000
in other words,

00:22:57.000 --> 00:22:58.000
what God is not asking

00:22:58.000 --> 00:22:59.000
permission from somebody.

00:22:59.000 --> 00:23:00.000
You know?

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:01.000
One second, gentlemen.

00:23:01.000 --> 00:23:02.000
You have to be,

00:23:04.000 --> 00:23:05.000
you have to be patient.

00:23:06.000 --> 00:23:07.000
You have to be patient.

00:23:08.000 --> 00:23:09.000
And you have to let me finish.

00:23:09.000 --> 00:23:10.000
And then,

00:23:10.000 --> 00:23:11.000
you know,

00:23:11.000 --> 00:23:12.000
I'm aware of other expressions,

00:23:12.000 --> 00:23:13.000
but let me give you first

00:23:13.000 --> 00:23:14.000
the Peshat.

00:23:14.000 --> 00:23:15.000
The Peshat is the following.

00:23:15.000 --> 00:23:16.000
God, in this word,

00:23:16.000 --> 00:23:17.000
na'ase adam

00:23:17.000 --> 00:23:18.000
besamero kibutenu,

00:23:18.000 --> 00:23:19.000
is telling us

00:23:20.000 --> 00:23:21.000
that He planned

00:23:22.000 --> 00:23:23.000
man.

00:23:23.000 --> 00:23:24.000
The creation of man

00:23:24.000 --> 00:23:25.000
was with a design.

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:26.000
God has a special design.

00:23:26.000 --> 00:23:27.000
Now, of course,

00:23:27.000 --> 00:23:28.000
for everything,

00:23:28.000 --> 00:23:29.000
God has a special design.

00:23:29.000 --> 00:23:30.000
But only for man,

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:31.000
the Bible makes it clear

00:23:32.000 --> 00:23:33.000
that there was a special design

00:23:34.000 --> 00:23:35.000
for the creation of man.

00:23:36.000 --> 00:23:37.000
Now, how does God

00:23:37.000 --> 00:23:38.000
speak to Himself?

00:23:39.000 --> 00:23:40.000
You know?

00:23:40.000 --> 00:23:41.000
God speaks to Himself,

00:23:41.000 --> 00:23:42.000
na'ase adam

00:23:42.000 --> 00:23:43.000
besamero kibutenu.

00:23:43.000 --> 00:23:44.000
Let us make.

00:23:44.000 --> 00:23:45.000
This is the expression

00:23:45.000 --> 00:23:47.000
which I personally accept

00:23:47.000 --> 00:23:49.000
as the Peshat of the verse.

00:23:49.000 --> 00:23:50.000
These other expressions,

00:23:50.000 --> 00:23:51.000
I will tell you in a second.

00:23:51.000 --> 00:23:52.000
All right?

00:23:52.000 --> 00:23:53.000
But the first expression is,

00:23:53.000 --> 00:23:54.000
na'ase adam

00:23:54.000 --> 00:23:55.000
besamero kibutenu.

00:23:56.000 --> 00:23:57.000
It means,

00:23:57.000 --> 00:23:58.000
that is the way that God speaks

00:23:58.000 --> 00:23:59.000
because majesty

00:23:59.000 --> 00:24:00.000
speaks in plural.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:01.000
That is the proper derech-eres

00:24:01.000 --> 00:24:02.000
according to the Bible

00:24:02.000 --> 00:24:03.000
to speak.

00:24:03.000 --> 00:24:04.000
As a matter of fact,

00:24:04.000 --> 00:24:05.000
you need to go to the Bible.

00:24:05.000 --> 00:24:06.000
You go to the television.

00:24:06.000 --> 00:24:07.000
When Nixon speaks,

00:24:07.000 --> 00:24:08.000
he says,

00:24:08.000 --> 00:24:09.000
we think,

00:24:09.000 --> 00:24:10.000
always speaks in plural.

00:24:10.000 --> 00:24:11.000
Why?

00:24:11.000 --> 00:24:12.000
He is the president of the nation

00:24:12.000 --> 00:24:13.000
and therefore he speaks

00:24:13.000 --> 00:24:14.000
in plural.

00:24:18.000 --> 00:24:19.000
All right.

00:24:19.000 --> 00:24:20.000
That's right.

00:24:20.000 --> 00:24:21.000
Now, why?

00:24:21.000 --> 00:24:22.000
Because I said

00:24:22.000 --> 00:24:23.000
why it speaks in plural

00:24:23.000 --> 00:24:24.000
because only in Adam,

00:24:24.000 --> 00:24:25.000
God is telling us

00:24:26.000 --> 00:24:27.000
what He thought

00:24:27.000 --> 00:24:28.000
before He created Him.

00:24:29.000 --> 00:24:30.000
That's one expression.

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:31.000
Second expression,

00:24:31.000 --> 00:24:32.000
and that's the more popular expression

00:24:32.000 --> 00:24:33.000
and you could accept it,

00:24:33.000 --> 00:24:34.000
I think it also makes a lot of sense,

00:24:35.000 --> 00:24:36.000
is the following.

00:24:36.000 --> 00:24:37.000
God is speaking to all creation

00:24:39.000 --> 00:24:40.000
and in the creation

00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:41.000
there are many elements

00:24:41.000 --> 00:24:42.000
in the creation.

00:24:42.000 --> 00:24:43.000
There is the mineral,

00:24:43.000 --> 00:24:44.000
there is the vegetable,

00:24:45.000 --> 00:24:46.000
there is also the soul

00:24:46.000 --> 00:24:47.000
which belongs to the angel

00:24:47.000 --> 00:24:48.000
and therefore God is speaking

00:24:48.000 --> 00:24:49.000
to all creation

00:24:49.000 --> 00:24:50.000
and says to creation as a whole,

00:24:51.000 --> 00:24:52.000
let us make something

00:24:53.000 --> 00:24:54.000
that encompasses

00:24:55.000 --> 00:24:56.000
all of creation.

00:24:57.000 --> 00:24:58.000
A micro,

00:24:59.000 --> 00:25:00.000
a mini world.

00:25:01.000 --> 00:25:02.000
A mini world

00:25:02.000 --> 00:25:03.000
that is going to be

00:25:03.000 --> 00:25:04.000
Adam.

00:25:04.000 --> 00:25:05.000
In other words,

00:25:05.000 --> 00:25:06.000
God is speaking

00:25:06.000 --> 00:25:07.000
to the whole rest of the world

00:25:07.000 --> 00:25:08.000
that He created.

00:25:08.000 --> 00:25:09.000
Let us make

00:25:09.000 --> 00:25:10.000
out of ourselves

00:25:10.000 --> 00:25:11.000
and each one gives a little.

00:25:11.000 --> 00:25:12.000
You know?

00:25:14.000 --> 00:25:15.000
That is the most standard

00:25:15.000 --> 00:25:16.000
explanation

00:25:16.000 --> 00:25:17.000
and this man

00:25:17.000 --> 00:25:18.000
you will have

00:25:18.000 --> 00:25:19.000
from everything.

00:25:19.000 --> 00:25:20.000
You have from the animal,

00:25:20.000 --> 00:25:21.000
you have from the vegetable,

00:25:21.000 --> 00:25:22.000
you have from this,

00:25:22.000 --> 00:25:23.000
you have from that

00:25:23.000 --> 00:25:24.000
and you have a little bit

00:25:24.000 --> 00:25:25.000
from God.

00:25:25.000 --> 00:25:26.000
You see?

00:25:27.000 --> 00:25:28.000
All the same,

00:25:28.000 --> 00:25:29.000
everything

00:25:29.000 --> 00:25:30.000
it is found in man.

00:25:31.000 --> 00:25:32.000
That explanation

00:25:33.000 --> 00:25:34.000
is the most

00:25:35.000 --> 00:25:36.000
accepted explanation

00:25:36.000 --> 00:25:37.000
in Jewish circles.

00:25:37.000 --> 00:25:38.000
Do you understand?

00:25:38.000 --> 00:25:39.000
It is a nice explanation

00:25:40.000 --> 00:25:41.000
that man encompasses

00:25:41.000 --> 00:25:42.000
all of creation.

00:25:42.000 --> 00:25:43.000
Yes?

00:25:43.000 --> 00:25:44.000
And the word Adam?

00:25:54.000 --> 00:25:55.000
Well, excuse me.

00:25:56.000 --> 00:25:57.000
No,

00:25:57.000 --> 00:25:58.000
we have Trinity,

00:25:58.000 --> 00:25:59.000
you know,

00:25:59.000 --> 00:26:00.000
down here.

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:01.000
I mean,

00:26:01.000 --> 00:26:02.000
not here.

00:26:02.000 --> 00:26:03.000
A little bit far from here.

00:26:06.000 --> 00:26:07.000
I cannot reject Trinity

00:26:07.000 --> 00:26:08.000
if I am a good,

00:26:08.000 --> 00:26:09.000
you know.

00:26:17.000 --> 00:26:18.000
Oh,

00:26:18.000 --> 00:26:19.000
since there is

00:26:19.000 --> 00:26:20.000
a tape recorder,

00:26:20.000 --> 00:26:21.000
I would say,

00:26:21.000 --> 00:26:22.000
of course,

00:26:22.000 --> 00:26:23.000
I reject it.

00:26:26.000 --> 00:26:27.000
I beg your pardon?

00:26:28.000 --> 00:26:29.000
The angels,

00:26:29.000 --> 00:26:30.000
and this is true,

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:31.000
I believe the Peshad,

00:26:31.000 --> 00:26:32.000
that says like this.

00:26:36.000 --> 00:26:37.000
See, the Ramban,

00:26:37.000 --> 00:26:38.000
the greatest,

00:26:38.000 --> 00:26:39.000
you see,

00:26:39.000 --> 00:26:40.000
I am talking about Kabbalah,

00:26:40.000 --> 00:26:41.000
it is important to know

00:26:41.000 --> 00:26:42.000
a little bit about Kabbalah

00:26:42.000 --> 00:26:43.000
and there is the following.

00:26:43.000 --> 00:26:44.000
You have many people

00:26:44.000 --> 00:26:45.000
talking about Kabbalah

00:26:45.000 --> 00:26:46.000
and there is many explanations

00:26:46.000 --> 00:26:47.000
what Kabbalah is and so on.

00:26:47.000 --> 00:26:48.000
The greatest Mikubalim,

00:26:48.000 --> 00:26:49.000
and among them

00:26:49.000 --> 00:26:50.000
was the Ramban,

00:26:50.000 --> 00:26:51.000
Rav Moshe Bar Nahman,

00:26:51.000 --> 00:26:52.000
was a Sephardi.

00:26:52.000 --> 00:26:53.000
He says,

00:26:53.000 --> 00:26:54.000
look,

00:26:55.000 --> 00:26:56.000
the Torah

00:26:56.000 --> 00:26:57.000
is written for everyone.

00:26:58.000 --> 00:26:59.000
You know?

00:26:59.000 --> 00:27:00.000
And the object of the Torah,

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:01.000
the Peshad of the Torah,

00:27:01.000 --> 00:27:02.000
is to reach

00:27:02.000 --> 00:27:04.000
every single individual.

00:27:04.000 --> 00:27:05.000
It is not written

00:27:05.000 --> 00:27:06.000
in the Torah

00:27:06.000 --> 00:27:07.000
only for the few chosen

00:27:07.000 --> 00:27:09.000
geniuses of the world.

00:27:09.000 --> 00:27:10.000
No.

00:27:10.000 --> 00:27:11.000
The Torah is written

00:27:11.000 --> 00:27:12.000
for every single one.

00:27:12.000 --> 00:27:13.000
So therefore,

00:27:13.000 --> 00:27:14.000
what about Malakhim?

00:27:14.000 --> 00:27:15.000
Malakhim is not something

00:27:15.000 --> 00:27:16.000
that everyone

00:27:16.000 --> 00:27:17.000
needs to know

00:27:17.000 --> 00:27:19.000
or is important for them.

00:27:19.000 --> 00:27:20.000
It is only for those

00:27:20.000 --> 00:27:21.000
who want to study Kabbalah

00:27:21.000 --> 00:27:22.000
and for them

00:27:22.000 --> 00:27:23.000
there is another branch.

00:27:23.000 --> 00:27:24.000
Therefore,

00:27:24.000 --> 00:27:25.000
the Torah does not speak

00:27:25.000 --> 00:27:26.000
about Malakhim,

00:27:26.000 --> 00:27:27.000
the creation of Malakhim.

00:27:27.000 --> 00:27:28.000
Why?

00:27:28.000 --> 00:27:29.000
Because that creation

00:27:29.000 --> 00:27:30.000
of Malakhim

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:31.000
is not relevant

00:27:31.000 --> 00:27:33.000
for the coming person.

00:27:33.000 --> 00:27:35.000
It is not important.

00:27:35.000 --> 00:27:36.000
You know?

00:27:36.000 --> 00:27:37.000
It is a supernatural.

00:27:37.000 --> 00:27:38.000
The Torah comes

00:27:38.000 --> 00:27:40.000
to speak for everyone.

00:27:40.000 --> 00:27:41.000
And this is important

00:27:41.000 --> 00:27:42.000
to remember this.

00:27:42.000 --> 00:27:43.000
And that is the uniqueness

00:27:43.000 --> 00:27:44.000
of the Jewish people

00:27:44.000 --> 00:27:45.000
is that every Jew

00:27:45.000 --> 00:27:46.000
is equal

00:27:46.000 --> 00:27:47.000
and every Jew

00:27:47.000 --> 00:27:49.000
should be equally educated.

00:27:49.000 --> 00:27:50.000
In other words,

00:27:50.000 --> 00:27:51.000
education is not,

00:27:51.000 --> 00:27:52.000
you know,

00:27:52.000 --> 00:27:53.000
the way

00:27:53.000 --> 00:27:54.000
that only the very few

00:27:54.000 --> 00:27:55.000
could read it.

00:27:55.000 --> 00:27:56.000
The Torah was not

00:27:56.000 --> 00:27:57.000
written in this way.

00:27:57.000 --> 00:27:58.000
Why?

00:27:58.000 --> 00:27:59.000
Because again,

00:27:59.000 --> 00:28:00.000
it should be for everyone.

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:01.000
And that is why

00:28:01.000 --> 00:28:02.000
Malakhim,

00:28:02.000 --> 00:28:03.000
the creation of Malakhim,

00:28:03.000 --> 00:28:04.000
the creation of many

00:28:04.000 --> 00:28:05.000
other things

00:28:05.000 --> 00:28:06.000
are not mentioned

00:28:06.000 --> 00:28:07.000
in the Torah

00:28:07.000 --> 00:28:08.000
because not everyone

00:28:08.000 --> 00:28:09.000
could understand it.

00:28:09.000 --> 00:28:10.000
Kabbalah?

00:28:10.000 --> 00:28:11.000
That is another

00:28:11.000 --> 00:28:12.000
explanation

00:28:12.000 --> 00:28:13.000
that God was speaking

00:28:13.000 --> 00:28:14.000
to the angels.

00:28:14.000 --> 00:28:15.000
Yes.

00:28:15.000 --> 00:28:16.000
But this explanation

00:28:16.000 --> 00:28:17.000
that you have given

00:28:17.000 --> 00:28:18.000
is part of the other

00:28:18.000 --> 00:28:19.000
explanation

00:28:19.000 --> 00:28:20.000
which I gave

00:28:20.000 --> 00:28:21.000
that God is talking

00:28:21.000 --> 00:28:22.000
and saying,

00:28:22.000 --> 00:28:23.000
let us make a man

00:28:23.000 --> 00:28:24.000
that this man,

00:28:24.000 --> 00:28:25.000
a creation that should

00:28:25.000 --> 00:28:26.000
reflect the whole

00:28:26.000 --> 00:28:27.000
universe and earth

00:28:27.000 --> 00:28:28.000
and that is why

00:28:28.000 --> 00:28:29.000
man was called

00:28:29.000 --> 00:28:30.000
the microcosm

00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:31.000
which means

00:28:31.000 --> 00:28:32.000
olam katan

00:28:32.000 --> 00:28:33.000
the small little world

00:28:33.000 --> 00:28:34.000
because it encompasses

00:28:34.000 --> 00:28:35.000
the whole creation.

00:28:35.000 --> 00:28:36.000
Is it not possible

00:28:36.000 --> 00:28:37.000
that the whole concept

00:28:37.000 --> 00:28:38.000
of Kabbalah

00:28:38.000 --> 00:28:39.000
is a product

00:28:39.000 --> 00:28:40.000
of the fertile

00:28:40.000 --> 00:28:41.000
imagination

00:28:41.000 --> 00:28:42.000
of man

00:28:42.000 --> 00:28:43.000
and possibly

00:28:43.000 --> 00:28:44.000
has no connection

00:28:44.000 --> 00:28:45.000
whatever with the Torah?

00:28:45.000 --> 00:28:46.000
Well,

00:28:46.000 --> 00:28:47.000
I believe

00:28:47.000 --> 00:28:48.000
in one part

00:28:48.000 --> 00:28:49.000
what you said

00:28:49.000 --> 00:28:50.000
and I reject

00:28:50.000 --> 00:28:51.000
the other.

00:28:51.000 --> 00:28:52.000
I believe

00:28:52.000 --> 00:28:53.000
that it is part

00:28:53.000 --> 00:28:54.000
of the imagination.

00:28:54.000 --> 00:28:55.000
Yes.

00:28:55.000 --> 00:28:56.000
But again,

00:28:56.000 --> 00:28:57.000
for us,

00:28:57.000 --> 00:28:58.000
the imagination

00:28:58.000 --> 00:28:59.000
in Judaism

00:28:59.000 --> 00:29:00.000
is also good.

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:01.000
In other words,

00:29:01.000 --> 00:29:02.000
not only the intellect

00:29:02.000 --> 00:29:03.000
but also the imaginative

00:29:03.000 --> 00:29:04.000
part of man,

00:29:04.000 --> 00:29:05.000
the imaginative faculty

00:29:05.000 --> 00:29:06.000
of man is important.

00:29:06.000 --> 00:29:07.000
In Haramban,

00:29:07.000 --> 00:29:08.000
by the way,

00:29:08.000 --> 00:29:09.000
he thinks that Kabbalah

00:29:09.000 --> 00:29:10.000
could be only understood

00:29:10.000 --> 00:29:11.000
not through the intellect

00:29:11.000 --> 00:29:12.000
but through the imagination.

00:29:12.000 --> 00:29:13.000
But however,

00:29:13.000 --> 00:29:14.000
I believe

00:29:14.000 --> 00:29:15.000
that there is

00:29:15.000 --> 00:29:16.000
such a thing

00:29:16.000 --> 00:29:17.000
as a Kabbalah

00:29:17.000 --> 00:29:18.000
and I believe

00:29:18.000 --> 00:29:19.000
that in the Torah

00:29:19.000 --> 00:29:20.000
there are

00:29:20.000 --> 00:29:21.000
very elements

00:29:21.000 --> 00:29:22.000
of Kabbalah

00:29:22.000 --> 00:29:23.000
in the Torah.

00:29:23.000 --> 00:29:24.000
I believe

00:29:24.000 --> 00:29:25.000
that we always had

00:29:25.000 --> 00:29:26.000
Mekubalim

00:29:26.000 --> 00:29:27.000
and that there is

00:29:27.000 --> 00:29:28.000
such a thing

00:29:28.000 --> 00:29:29.000
as a genuine

00:29:29.000 --> 00:29:30.000
esoteric meaning

00:29:30.000 --> 00:29:31.000
to the Torah.

00:29:31.000 --> 00:29:32.000
However,

00:29:32.000 --> 00:29:33.000
what I don't accept

00:29:33.000 --> 00:29:34.000
is that everyone today

00:29:34.000 --> 00:29:35.000
who says

00:29:35.000 --> 00:29:36.000
I'm Mekubal,

00:29:36.000 --> 00:29:37.000
Mekubal,

00:29:37.000 --> 00:29:38.000
this I don't accept.

00:29:38.000 --> 00:29:39.000
Every Tom and Dick

00:29:39.000 --> 00:29:40.000
who says

00:29:40.000 --> 00:29:41.000
I'm Mekubal,

00:29:41.000 --> 00:29:42.000
this I don't accept

00:29:42.000 --> 00:29:43.000
but I do accept

00:29:43.000 --> 00:29:44.000
that there is

00:29:44.000 --> 00:29:45.000
such a thing

00:29:45.000 --> 00:29:46.000
as Kabbalah

00:29:46.000 --> 00:29:47.000
and Kabbalah

00:29:47.000 --> 00:29:48.000
is worthwhile

00:29:48.000 --> 00:29:49.000
because they are

00:29:49.000 --> 00:29:50.000
not only capable

00:29:50.000 --> 00:29:51.000
in the sense

00:29:51.000 --> 00:29:52.000
intellectually

00:29:52.000 --> 00:29:53.000
also they are

00:29:53.000 --> 00:29:54.000
in the proper atmosphere.

00:29:54.000 --> 00:29:55.000
I don't think

00:29:55.000 --> 00:29:56.000
that nobody

00:29:56.000 --> 00:29:57.000
could study Kabbalah

00:29:57.000 --> 00:29:58.000
in the United States

00:29:58.000 --> 00:29:59.000
of America.

00:29:59.000 --> 00:30:00.000
It's impossible.

00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:01.000
How could you study Kabbalah

00:30:01.000 --> 00:30:02.000
and walk in the streets?

00:30:02.000 --> 00:30:03.000
Impossible.

00:30:03.000 --> 00:30:04.000
For me,

00:30:04.000 --> 00:30:05.000
anyone who tells me

00:30:05.000 --> 00:30:06.000
that the study is

00:30:06.000 --> 00:30:07.000
I don't believe this.

00:30:07.000 --> 00:30:08.000
You need a proper atmosphere,

00:30:08.000 --> 00:30:09.000
you need a proper place

00:30:09.000 --> 00:30:10.000
and what is more important

00:30:10.000 --> 00:30:11.000
the proper teacher.

00:30:11.000 --> 00:30:12.000
You cannot study

00:30:12.000 --> 00:30:13.000
Kabbalah

00:30:13.000 --> 00:30:14.000
on your own.

00:30:14.000 --> 00:30:15.000
You have to have

00:30:15.000 --> 00:30:16.000
your proper teacher.

00:30:16.000 --> 00:30:17.000
If you don't have

00:30:17.000 --> 00:30:18.000
a proper teacher

00:30:18.000 --> 00:30:19.000
you will be

00:30:19.000 --> 00:30:20.000
stumbling,

00:30:20.000 --> 00:30:21.000
you may think

00:30:21.000 --> 00:30:22.000
that you know a lot

00:30:22.000 --> 00:30:23.000
but in fact

00:30:23.000 --> 00:30:24.000
that is pure imagination

00:30:24.000 --> 00:30:25.000
as Mr. Sitton said

00:30:25.000 --> 00:30:26.000
that has nothing

00:30:26.000 --> 00:30:27.000
to do with Kabbalah.

00:30:27.000 --> 00:30:28.000
This is the imagination

00:30:28.000 --> 00:30:29.000
that some people

00:30:29.000 --> 00:30:30.000
they think

00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:31.000
that they know

00:30:31.000 --> 00:30:32.000
Kabbalah

00:30:32.000 --> 00:30:33.000
and so on.

00:30:33.000 --> 00:30:34.000
I don't accept,

00:30:34.000 --> 00:30:35.000
sir.

00:30:35.000 --> 00:30:36.000
It seems awkward

00:30:36.000 --> 00:30:37.000
to me

00:30:37.000 --> 00:30:38.000
that he creates

00:30:38.000 --> 00:30:39.000
man over here

00:30:39.000 --> 00:30:40.000
Adam

00:30:40.000 --> 00:30:41.000
in his image.

00:30:41.000 --> 00:30:42.000
We didn't say

00:30:42.000 --> 00:30:43.000
still what it means

00:30:43.000 --> 00:30:44.000
image.

00:30:44.000 --> 00:30:45.000
We didn't explain

00:30:45.000 --> 00:30:46.000
what the image means.

00:30:47.000 --> 00:30:48.000
It is more important

00:30:48.000 --> 00:30:49.000
perhaps

00:30:49.000 --> 00:30:50.000
than all the other creations.

00:30:50.000 --> 00:30:51.000
It is very important

00:30:51.000 --> 00:30:52.000
because it is Salman.

00:30:52.000 --> 00:30:53.000
What does it mean Salman?

00:30:53.000 --> 00:30:54.000
I will explain to you

00:30:54.000 --> 00:30:55.000
in a second.

00:30:55.000 --> 00:30:56.000
But he neglects

00:30:56.000 --> 00:30:57.000
to even say

00:30:57.000 --> 00:30:58.000
man's purpose.

00:30:58.000 --> 00:30:59.000
It would seem

00:30:59.000 --> 00:31:00.000
that he should

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:01.000
